('area:tignes-val-disere','explore','line',10,'Pages for Tignes, Val d''Isère and their villages come next, with the runs, ski schools, restaurants and places to stay that this page leaves out.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','explore.2.text'),
('area:tignes-val-disere','method','line',0,'Which resorts count','{}'::text[],'review','loader','method.items.0.dt'),
('area:tignes-val-disere','method','line',1,'Tignes and Val d''Isère, the two resorts on the Tignes Val d''Isère pass, split into the eight sectors that a skier meets on the ground. Sharing the pass is recorded separately from being linked by lift and piste.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','method.items.0.dd'),
('area:tignes-val-disere','method','line',2,'How links were checked','{}'::text[],'review','loader','method.items.1.dt'),
('area:tignes-val-disere','method','line',3,'A sector counts as linked only when a route of lifts and pistes reaches it in the OpenStreetMap data. Drag lifts run one way, gondolas and the two funiculars may be ridden down, and the walks from the underground Perce-Neige stations and along the Val Claret snow front are added by hand. A link is critical when closing one lift on it cuts routes that no other lift replaces. The model has not yet been checked against the official 2026/27 piste map.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','method.items.1.dd'),
('area:tignes-val-disere','method','line',4,'Piste totals','{}'::text[],'review','loader','method.items.2.dt'),
('area:tignes-val-disere','method','line',5,'Operator and measured figures are both shown and never averaged. Mapped piste from OpenStreetMap is used only to compare sectors and grades.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','method.items.2.dd'),
('area:tignes-val-disere','method','line',6,'Comparisons','{}'::text[],'review','loader','method.items.3.dt'),
('area:tignes-val-disere','method','line',7,'The four areas compared use the same source for each row, so a figure can be set against its neighbour.','{}'::text[],'review','loader','method.items.3.dd'),
